Third-Party Attribution
=======================

This product is built from open-source components. Full license texts for all
third-party crates compiled into Hearth are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

A complete list of crates and their SPDX identifiers can be reproduced at any
time by running:

    cargo deny list             # license summary
    make notice                 # regenerate THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES from Cargo.lock

No third-party crate in Hearth's current dependency tree ships its own NOTICE
file. If that changes as dependencies are updated, run `make notice` and commit
both THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES and this file with the updated attribution text.

Key cryptographic dependencies and their provenance:

  ring 0.17.x
    BoringSSL (portions) — ISC / OpenSSL / MIT hybrid license.
    BoringSSL itself contains code derived from OpenSSL.
    See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES for the full ring license text.

  aws-lc-rs / aws-lc-sys
    AWS-LC — Apache-2.0.
    AWS-LC is a general-purpose cryptographic library maintained by AWS.
    Based in part on BoringSSL.
    See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES for the full aws-lc-rs and aws-lc-sys license text.

  rustls 0.23.x
    Apache-2.0 / MIT / ISC (your choice).
    See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES for the full text.

